{"id":"assistant-a1f15531-2105-58ca-85d0-1f62c7ca7255","sessionId":"5ee34cd6-1b7a-ca34-23cd-358c218ae0a4","turnId":"turn-a7fbac27e592da78e7f88f344abedbda","inputEntryId":"user-turn-a7fbac27e592da78e7f88f344abedbda-1","createdAt":1794276944335,"updatedAt":1794276944335,"generationStatus":"completed","relatedEntryId":null,"type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done.\n\n**Summary:**\n\n- **Root cause:** The `similarity()` function returns a Python `float` (from `round()`), which DynamoDB rejects. First publish works (empty table = no similarity computed), second publish fails (existing data triggers similarity calculation with floats).\n\n- **Fix:** Changed `similarity()` in `src/app.py` to return `int(round((0.7 * tag_score + 0.3 * word_score) * 10000))` — scaling the score to an integer that DynamoDB accepts.\n\n- **Test:** Added `test_publish_with_existing_story` in `tests/test_publish.py` that seeds the table before the second write, exercising the state-dependent code path.\n\n- **ANSWER.md:** Created with full explanation of cause, fix, and which parts of the colleague's note applied (nearly all of them)."}],"source":"harness","userDisplayContent":null,"outcome":{"type":"committed"}}
